  "id": "attitude-change",
  "term": "attitude change",
  "definition": "Attitude change is a shift in a person’s stated attitude, such as after acting in a way that goes against their original view. In cognitive dissonance research, this change is commonly studied after counter-attitudinal behavior and is linked to emotions, with more positive emotions and fewer negative emotions associated with greater change.",
